2. The `binarySearch` function implements the binary search algorithm, which works by repeatedly dividing the search interval in half. The algorithm compares the middle element of the interval with the target value. If they are equal, the search is complete. If the middle element is greater than the target value, the algorithm searches the left half of the interval. Otherwise, it searches the right half of the interval.

3. In the main function, we first prompt the user to enter the length and the elements of the array.

