import java.util.Scanner;

public class PalindromeRecursion {

    public static boolean isPalindrome(String str) {
        if (str.length() == 0 || str.length() == 1) {
            return true;
        }

        if (str.charAt(0) == str.charAt(str.length() - 1)) {
            return isPalindrome(str.substring(1, str.length() - 1));
        }

        return false;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        System.out.print("Enter a string: ");
        String str = sc.nextLine();

        if (isPalindrome(str)) {
            System.out.println(str + " is a palindrome");
        } else {
            System.out.println(str + " is not a palindrome");
        }
    }
}
```

The `isPalindrome()` method takes a string argument and recursively checks whether the first and last characters are equal. If they are, the method is called again with the substring between the first and last characters. If not, the string is not a palindrome.

